 //   dst[0] y       [n_ch, 1] F32, silu(conv)
 //   dst[1] slot    the same tensor as src[4], listed for the dirty tracking of the cache
 //
-// A slot has the layout of the CONCAT input without the new column: for each channel, 3 floats in
-// time order (s0, s1, s2). The new slot of a channel holds (s1, s2, x).
+// A slot holds three planes of n_ch floats. Plane t holds tap t of every channel, in time order:
+// plane 0 is the oldest column, plane 2 the newest. The new slot of a channel holds (s1, s2, x).
 //
-// The kernel is HVX only. It reads DDR with unaligned vector loads, keeps everything in registers,
-// and writes DDR with unaligned vector stores. Scalar code never touches the data: scalar access to
-// VTCM is slow, and the layout change from 3 lanes per channel to 4 lanes per channel is done with
-// rotates and masks. For a block of 32 channels:
-//   1. The 96 slot lanes and the 32 column lanes become 4 vectors c[g] with lane 4k + t = tap t of
-//      channel 8g + k (t = 3 is the new column).
-//   2. Four vdeal ops split c[0..3] into the tap planes t0..t3 (lane = channel). The weights get
-//      the same split.
+// The kernel is HVX only, and it keeps everything in registers. The plane layout gives each tap of
+// a block of 32 channels its own vector, thus the kernel loads the taps, and writes the new slot,
+// without a lane permutation. For a block of 32 channels:
+//   1. Load the three tap planes and the new column: t0, t1, t2, t3 (lane = channel).
+//   2. Four vdeal ops split the 128 weight lanes into the tap planes w0..w3 (lane = channel).
 //   3. acc = t0 * w0, acc += t1 * w1, acc += t2 * w2, acc += t3 * w3: the sum of the CPU reference
 //      (ggml_compute_forward_ssm_conv_f32) in the same order.
 //   4. y = acc * sigmoid(acc) with the two routines of the SILU op of this backend.
-//   5. The new slot lanes (s1, s2, x) of each channel come from c[g] with rotates and masks.
+//   5. The new slot planes are (t1, t2, t3), thus three stores of registers that are already there.
+//
+// The previous layout of a slot was 3 floats per channel in time order. The conversion of that
+// layout to the tap planes, and back, cost approximately 200 of the 270 vector ops of a block, and
+// the permute unit of the HVX was the limit of the op. The row size of a slot does not change.
+//
+// The host must write the conv state cache in this layout. The state of a sequence is only read
+// and written by this op, thus the layout is internal to the backend. But the host must convert
+// the layout when it serializes the state of a session (llama_state_get_data and
+// llama_state_set_data), and when a layer of the model falls back to a different backend.
 
